{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792667341,"nonce":"5/w2Xe39SLmBgCgvxQ7QeASh21o=","title":"code-diff: the Stage and Revert buttons show on hover only, so the keyboard cannot reach them","message":"Found while building the diff view (ed51114).\n\n**What happens**\n\nThe buttons on the first row of a change are `visibility: hidden` until the pointer is over the row, which keeps them off the code. A hidden element cannot take focus, so a keyboard user can scroll through changes with F7 but cannot stage or revert one.\n\n**What is wanted**\n\nA way to reach them by keyboard: for example, F7 and Shift+F7 move a current-change marker, and Enter, or a letter, runs the Stage hook on the current change; or the buttons show when the row or the change is the current one. The buttons being hooks (`onStage`, `onRevert`, `hunkActions`) keeps this a view concern.","files":null}]}